WEBVTT

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.640
Kitakado-kun, look this way.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.520
That's nice.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.400
Korekuni-kun, try leaning 
against Kitakado-kun.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.210
Okay. Let's take a break 
to check the shots we got.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.110
I heard the recording, Tsubasa-chan.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.370
Kitakore's new song turned out well.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:26.040
Really?

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.340
Yeah, really.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.340
Everyone at the office agrees, too.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.290
That's great.

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:37.340
Apparently, the boys of MooNs heard it, too.

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.320
They were excitedly saying they'd 
record a song just as good.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.270
It's lighter than I thought.

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.830
That's the one that got 
them the commercial deal, right?

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.270
How's this?

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.210
That's right. They're on the verge 
of appearing in the commercial now.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:46.370
Thanks.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:47.850
No problem.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.210
The inner material is really nice, too.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:56.530
Tsubasa-chan, go knock this THRIVE 
production meeting out of the park, too.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.180
I'll do my best.

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:04.170
Listen, it's your job to push 
those B-Pro boys forward.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:05.560
Got it.

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:39.240
<b><i>The BAD END Isn't So Bad</i></b>

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.270
Wh-What should we do?

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.330
Maybe another listen—

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.070
It doesn't matter how many times we listen. 
It won't change my opinion.

00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:02.280
This arrangement won't work. 
We need to be louder.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.190
You're still going on about that?

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:07.760
You're a professional. You need 
to accept things for what they are.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.660
Accept that this is just a job.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:13.290
Quit acting like a goody-two-shoes!

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.800
Unlike you, I'm an adult.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.800
U-Um...

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:23.010
Guys, don't fight.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.020
Gochin, it's our song. 
Let's talk about it, okay?

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:41.920
Leave him be. He's always like this.

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:43.370
Always?

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:46.950
Gochin doesn't like being an idol.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:50.060
He's like, "I don't see the point 
in sucking up more than I need to."

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:53.460
That kind of thinking
 is why he's a child.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:59.050
<i>THRIVE is totally different from Kitakore...</i>

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.390
This magazine's going to be 
doing an article on THRIVE.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:05.340
What?

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:10.180
<b>4 Angels Who Came 
From the Milky Way</b>

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:10.390
Wow! They're so brilliant.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.630
Hey, that's <i>Kiss & Hug</i>.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.680
Gochin hates these kinds of magazines.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:16.190
What?

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.650
The shoot is tomorrow.

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:23.070
I haven't told Goshi yet. That's your job.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.570
What?

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:32.540
Wow! This is where you live?

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:37.710
Yeah. Not just us, but look.

00:04:38.410 --> 00:04:39.340
Tsubasa.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:41.710
All of you live here, too?

00:04:42.440 --> 00:04:43.720
That's right.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:49.630
Daikoku Pro rents the upper levels 
of this building, so their clients can live here.

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.540
Each floor is home to a different group.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:56.730
Our boss demanded that his brother 
let him use the space since he's renting it,

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:59.980
which is why THRIVE lives here, too.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.320
Tsubasa?

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.830
<b>Daikoku Shuji</b>

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:08.810
They have the same last name!

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:13.130
Atsushi-san and Shuji-san are brothers.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:17.700
You just noticed?

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.370
You really are an airhead, Tsubasa.

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:23.580
Ba-dump. I like how slow 
on the uptake you are.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.720
It's cute.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:28.200
Is this your first time here, Tsubasa?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.180
Oh... Yes.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:32.140
Then allow me to properly welcome you.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.390
Welcome to our castle, princess.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:39.400
P-Princess?

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:41.030
As expected...

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:42.150
...from a prince.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:45.650
Shuji-san broke away from his brother

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:50.650
Atsushi's Daikoku Production to 
independently establish Brave Entertainment.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:54.870
Though his clients are still 
only THRIVE and one other group.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.860
I see.

00:05:57.860 --> 00:06:02.660
You're our A&R. You should 
at least know that much.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:04.610
Sorry.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.180
You don't need to apologize.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.610
How rare. Ryu-chan, 
nothing ever embarrasses you.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:16.090
I'm not embarrassed! 
Don't say things like that, Yuta!

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:20.060
Tsubasa, do you play any instruments?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:23.600
What? No, nothing.

00:06:24.090 --> 00:06:26.530
I just listen to music since I like it.

00:06:26.530 --> 00:06:27.830
What kind of music?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.030
Since I was little, I've listened 
to all kinds of music.

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.490
Some of it was probably 
my father's influence.

00:06:35.890 --> 00:06:40.250
I see. Maybe that's why 
your ears are so well-trained.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.380
Did something happen?

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:47.260
No, it's nothing.

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:50.130
Kaneshiro-san!

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:55.130
What is this? 
A gathering of lazy bums?

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.460
But we really don't have anything to do.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:07:00.350
Oh, you'll be busy tomorrow.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:05.110
Kaneshiro-san, you have 
a shoot for <i>Kiss & Hug</i>!

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:07.990
Oh, really?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:13.490
Yeah, about that. I wonder how 
many pages our article will be.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:17.490
I thought their offer was for 
a sexy dual-page photo of me.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:21.700
Oh, um... It's just one page.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.250
What? Just one page?

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:26.330
I don't have time for this.

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:29.380
Where are you going?

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:33.760
Probably to hide in the basement 
studio and play the guitar.

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:41.980
Kaneshiro-san will 
show up tomorrow, right?

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:45.600
He was really upset during 
the new song meeting.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:46.900
Don't worry about that.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:50.310
He hides in the studio to cool off.

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:55.700
Besides, despite everything he says, 
Gochin always does his job.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:58.290
So don't worry, Tsubasa-chan.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:01.200
Okay, thanks.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:05.790
I'll do my best to make 
B-Project a success.

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:10.920
Guys? Is something wrong?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.210
About B-Project...

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:18.510
Our individual groups are doing fairly well.

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:25.290
So why do we have to cut back on 
our groups' work to focus on B-Pro?

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:26.900
What?

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:31.900
But aren't the ten of you 
the primary members of B-Project?

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:36.150
Yashamaru-san said you were chosen 
from among ten thousand people.

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:43.040
But B-Pro was cut from the FMJ because 
there's little demand for us, right?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:48.060
In other words, nobody sees 
the appeal of B-Project.

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.250
That's the problem.

00:08:51.910 --> 00:08:54.580
You guys have been having 
deep thoughts like that?

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:57.570
I enjoy working with everybody.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.260
Yuta, you're too optimistic.

00:09:03.670 --> 00:09:07.520
<i>So that's how they feel about B-Project...</i>

00:09:16.690 --> 00:09:19.650
Is Yashamaru-san busy?

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.780
Hello, Ken Ken?

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:27.080
I finally found some limited 
edition rainbow pudding.

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:32.500
Yeah, yeah. You're calling me an idiot 
for taking a taxi to get some, right?

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.960
I'll be back soon. Don't be so upset.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:41.350
Yashamaru-san?

00:09:41.660 --> 00:09:45.410
And who's that woman?

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:51.480
Whatever.

00:09:52.890 --> 00:09:55.600
Sorry for the trouble.

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.200
It's fine. They wouldn't be 
THRIVE if they didn't fight.

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.700
Well, they do say the tougher a boy 
is to manage, the more endearing he is.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.590
Try facing down while 
looking up at me this time.

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:25.260
Kaneshiro-kun, let's try 
getting some cuter shots.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:28.560
Cuter? Seriously?

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:30.730
I don't get it.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:32.900
Kaneshiro-kun?

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:41.780
Gochin, you'll make me sad 
if you keep making a scary face.

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.030
Stop that, Ashu.

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:46.040
Come on. Come on.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:48.820
Nice, nice. That's it.

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:51.040
Bring the reflectors over here.

00:10:52.760 --> 00:10:54.050
Stop that, you idiot!

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.490
Good morning.

00:10:57.430 --> 00:10:58.880
How's it going?

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.780
You'd better be 
getting some good shots.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.310
Where are the Polaroids? 
Let me see them.

00:11:04.850 --> 00:11:07.930
And get me some coffee. 
Make sure it's hot.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:11.060
That's the editor-in-chief of <i>Kiss & Hug</i>.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:13.310
Really?

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:17.970
She seems arrogant. 
I don't like her.

00:11:18.400 --> 00:11:20.240
You're one to talk.

00:11:21.210 --> 00:11:24.490
<i>She seems familiar...</i>

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.300
Ashu-kun, look this way.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.750
Okay.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.250
What's with these boring photos?

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.060
Use those.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.110
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:35.630
Hurry up.

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.460
C-Cat ears?

00:11:39.460 --> 00:11:41.340
Put them on.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.170
What?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:44.050
<i>What?</i>

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:55.060
<i>K-Kaneshiro-san, you can do it...</i>

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:58.020
Quit wasting time. 
Hurry up and take some pictures.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:00.180
Show me some kitty cat poses.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:03.030
Okay!

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.210
Meow.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.380
You're next, Aizome-kun. Get in the shot.

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:09.910
Okay.

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:12.250
Meow, meow.

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:18.460
I came to see what they're like 
since they were really pushing them.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.770
It turns out they're not bad.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:29.380
What are you doing? 
Hurry up and put them on.

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:31.770
Meow, meow?

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:36.580
Yeah, don't you know? 
It's <i>Kiss & Hug</i>'s trademark pose.

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:38.710
If you want to be popular, you'll do it.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:44.280
If you can't do it yourself, I'll help you.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:45.990
Here.

00:12:48.810 --> 00:12:51.540
What's wrong? 
Hurry up and play like a cat.

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:56.250
Give me a cute meow.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.750
Come on. Meow, meow.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:12:59.750
I can't do that.

00:13:01.070 --> 00:13:01.510
What?

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:06.890
I won't wear these embarrassing things 
or appear in a THRIVE article!

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.640
Kaneshiro-san!

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:16.100
Do you know who you're talking to?

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:19.350
You're a perverted editor-in-chief
 with a cat ear fetish!

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:27.990
<i>K-K-Kaneshiro-san...</i>

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.160
Gochin was really mad.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.710
It'd be over so quickly if he would 
just stop complaining and do it.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.260
Here.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:40.640
Thanks.

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:41.920
Yay, thanks.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:43.300
This is chamomile tea.

00:13:45.400 --> 00:13:46.690
It smells nice.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:52.750
I made it. It'll help you relax, so I 
thought you could drink it during breaks.

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.480
What about Gochin? He needs 
this more than either of us.

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:59.310
He refused it. He said 
it smelled like grass.

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:04.820
When is the shoot going to resume?

00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:09.820
What's wrong with that Kaneshiro boy?

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.380
Make him do what I want.

00:14:12.380 --> 00:14:15.410
But if we're too forceful, it could 
affect future business with them.

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:17.680
Don't worry about that.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.220
Idols only last four or five years, anyway.

00:14:20.650 --> 00:14:21.260
Hey.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.040
Don't be ridiculous.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.810
Don't act like you can throw away 
idols once you're done with them.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:30.260
Oh, did I offend you? 
But isn't it true?

00:14:30.530 --> 00:14:36.210
Wear fashionable clothes, sing popular songs, 
and have girls scream over you.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:39.440
Isn't that all you boys want to do?

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.230
That's not what I want!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:45.350
Do you have any idea how many people 
you're inconveniencing with your selfishness?

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:48.900
You're just a little boy who 
doesn't understand anything.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.240
What did you say?

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:55.910
I'm telling you to take your pride 
and stay out of the way of the adults.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:14:58.940
All you need to do is smile.

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:01.690
The other two were doing it.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:04.890
Like a couple of idiots.

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:09.380
I'm canceling our deal 
with your crappy magazine!

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.240
But this isn't our first gravure magazine.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:13.820
What?

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.180
Gochin?

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:15.180
Goshi?

00:15:18.030 --> 00:15:19.430
That's what happened?

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:22.240
Yes. Anyway, um...

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:27.440
the editor-in-chief instructed us to swap out 
THRIVE for another artist for the article.

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:29.450
B-But...

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:32.840
What's gotten into you, Yuta?

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:36.630
I remember now. 
She was with Yashamaru-san.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:38.580
What are you talking about?

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:41.210
I saw them together.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:47.220
Does that mean Yashamaru-san 
was entertaining her?

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:47.920
What?

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.090
Yeah, that's right. Yashamaru-san 
works for Gandara, right?

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:56.540
He came to us a bunch 
of times to ask the editor-in-chief.

00:15:56.970 --> 00:15:59.980
"Just one page would do, so please 
put THRIVE in the magazine."

00:16:01.470 --> 00:16:03.060
Yashamaru-san did?

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.050
Yuta, let's look for Goshi.

00:16:06.490 --> 00:16:07.320
Yeah.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.740
I'll go with you, too.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.700
I promise we'll bring back 
Kaneshiro-san. So please...

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:19.370
Please don't let the 
editor-in-chief leave! Please!

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:25.960
<i>Where are you, Kaneshiro-san?</i>

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.740
<b>Daikoku Shuji
Urgent!</b>

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.270
There's something attached.

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:34.470
Version 2?

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.610
<i>This is the sound Kaneshiro-san requested.</i>

00:16:45.130 --> 00:16:50.510
<i>Shuji-san, Yashamaru-san and 
plenty of other people love THRIVE.</i>

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:52.230
<i>Kaneshiro-san...</i>

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.030
<i>Give me to the limit</i>

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.700
<i>Doesn't it invigorate your burning heart?</i>

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:04.000
<i>Overcoming the rampaging wind 
I'm always prepared ALL RIGHT</i>

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:05.960
<i>Going always</i>

00:17:05.960 --> 00:17:08.630
<i>The path that we've followed</i>

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:14.050
<i>Is overcoming our own unconventional selves</i>

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:19.510
<i>Frustrated by dissatisfying 
and incomplete answers</i>

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:27.520
<i>But don't turn away because beyond 
those obstacles lies a HAPPY END</i>

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:34.620
<i>So we don't miss the dream that's 
endlessly spreading out before us now</i>

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:31.350
He's not here.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:32.780
Tsubasa-chan!

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:34.280
I found Gochin!

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:38.370
<i>We'll pick up the pieces 
and put them together</i>

00:17:36.140 --> 00:17:36.970
Goshi!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:39.410
Kaneshiro-san!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:46.370
<i>Even the smallest lights someday</i>

00:17:39.880 --> 00:17:40.880
Wait, pl—

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:42.950
Tsubasa-chan!

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:42.950
Tsubasa!

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:55.730
<i>Break through the sky and become stars</i>

00:17:58.700 --> 00:17:59.510
You!

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.480
S-Sorry.

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:06.180
You used your body to stop Goshi? Not bad.

00:18:06.180 --> 00:18:08.660
What? I-I wasn't trying to...

00:18:10.950 --> 00:18:12.020
Goshi.

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:18.930
Yashamaru-san begged the 
editor-in-chief for today's job.

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:22.990
He had to ask the her a bunch of times.

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:38.960
Gochin!

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:39.510
Goshi!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:40.540
Kaneshiro-san!

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:47.210
Ma'am, can't you wait a little longer?

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:00.240
I'm sorry.

00:19:03.210 --> 00:19:05.780
Aizome-kun and Ashu-kun, right?

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:07.990
You'd be more popular

00:19:07.990 --> 00:19:11.240
if you dumped this pain in the ass 
and handled THRIVE on your own.

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:17.330
If it were just the two of you, I'd offer 
you an article on the rebirth of THRIVE.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:20.730
How does eight—no, ten pages sound?

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.810
No, thank you.

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:22.510
What?

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:26.770
Terrible things would happen 
if we let this pain in the ass run free.

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:28.910
We need to keep him on a leash.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:32.310
The three of us are THRIVE.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.570
Don't forget that.

00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:40.880
Wh-Wha...

00:19:41.400 --> 00:19:43.980
<i>Wh-Wh-Wh-What should I do?</i>

00:19:43.980 --> 00:19:45.580
Hello, everyone.

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:50.220
President Daikoku? 
What are you doing here?

00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:52.790
I had a meeting in the area.

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:55.750
I heard the editor-in-chief was here.

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.960
I came to see her. Right?

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:03.850
Are you finished with work for the day?

00:20:03.850 --> 00:20:06.660
Would you like to get dinner together?

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:07.670
Oh, my...

00:20:08.780 --> 00:20:11.270
You boys can handle the rest.

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.000
The shop called to let me know

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.820
they got some of the shizuku-zake 
I told you about the other day.

00:20:20.180 --> 00:20:22.150
Sorry about the wait.

00:20:22.150 --> 00:20:25.040
Please let us continue our photo shoot.

00:20:34.090 --> 00:20:35.630
Is this what you wanted?

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.270
Our new song is so cool.

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.010
Ah! You're still here?

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:52.890
Come here.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:56.350
Yeah, that's it. Over here. Huh?

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:57.430
Huh?

00:20:57.430 --> 00:20:59.300
He smelled one of his kind.

00:20:59.300 --> 00:20:59.940
What?

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:05.050
Let's take some shots with the cat.

00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:10.210
I couldn't say it in front 
of the editor-in-chief,

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:14.730
but honestly, I'm sick of that kitty pose.

00:21:17.820 --> 00:21:20.240
Hello? Yashamaru-san.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.200
Yes, things are okay here. 
We're almost finished.

00:21:25.490 --> 00:21:27.340
A powerful helper showed up to talk...

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:32.640
No, to meow some sense into him.

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:12.240
He doesn't make this face often.

00:23:12.470 --> 00:23:16.240
Yes. I think the article 
turned out wonderfully.

00:23:16.840 --> 00:23:21.250
But my brother didn't need to get involved.

00:23:23.170 --> 00:23:27.130
Oh, but the second version 
of the new song was wonderful.

00:23:27.920 --> 00:23:29.100
Of course it was.

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:30.670
Wrong!

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:32.890
Do your hands more like this!

00:23:33.150 --> 00:23:34.730
Make them rounder.

00:23:34.730 --> 00:23:37.310
And tilt your head a little.

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:39.770
Do I have to do this?

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:45.020
Of course. There's no telling when 
we'll be hired to do kitty poses again.

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:47.920
Right? Come on, Gochin.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:49.810
Let's kick it up a notch!

00:23:52.470 --> 00:23:54.210
Enough already.

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:01.000
<b>Let's Go With BRILLIANT</b>

00:23:55.690 --> 00:23:59.240
If you're going to sleep before me, that 
means that I can do anything I want, right?
